## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical fairness assessment, governance, and Azure OpenAI integration within a multi-tenant SaaS environment. It tests knowledge of KB grounding, per-tenant RBAC enforcement, and auditable logging under realistic enterprise constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Fairness metrics computed across tenant slices and inference outputs
- Guided prompting to reason about disparate impact patterns
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search over a versioned fairness knowledge base
- Per-tenant RBAC implementation using Azure AD
- Audit logging to Azure Data Lake for compliance
- Configurable remediation workflows triggered by fairness violations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Compute disparate impact ratio for a batch of model outputs
function computeDisparateImpact(outcomes, sensitiveAttribute) {
  const favorable = outcomes.filter(o => o.prediction === 1);
  const unfavorable = outcomes.filter(o => o.prediction === 0);

  const groupA = outcomes.filter(o => o[sensitiveAttribute] === 'A');
  const groupB = outcomes.filter(o => o[sensitiveAttribute] === 'B');

  const rateA = groupA.filter(o => o.prediction === 1).length / groupA.length;
  const rateB = groupB.filter(o => o.prediction === 1).length / groupB.length;

  // Disparate impact: ratio should be > 0.8 for fairness
  return Math.min(rateA, rateB) / Math.max(rateA, rateB);
}

// Example usage with tenant inference logs
const auditResult = computeDisparateImpact(tenantLogs, 'userSegment');
if (auditResult < 0.8) {
  triggerRemediation('data_rebalancing', auditResult);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes governance at scale: per-tenant safety, data residency, and cost-aware routing in a live Azure OpenAI pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-aware policy packs in blob storage
- PDP (policy decision point) in Azure Functions
- Data residency routing to OpenAI regional endpoints
- Redaction and guardrails before outbound calls
- Auditing and observability via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePDP(tenantId, metadata, policies) {
  const policy = policies[tenantId] || policies["default"];
  // residency check
  if (policy.residency && policy.residency !== metadata.region) return { action: "block" };
  // budget constraint
  if (typeof policy.budget === "number" && metadata.cost > policy.budget) return { action: "redirect", destination: "onPrem" };
  // allowed destination
  if (policy.allowedDestinations?.includes("OpenAI")) return { action: "allow", destination: "OpenAI" };
  return { action: "block" };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test PDP edge cases (missing tenant, malformed metadata, policy drift)?
- How would you implement zero-downtime policy updates and per-tenant rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
